{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2060","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Subtract Min Sort"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a sequence $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ positive integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can perform the following operation any number of times."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select an index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\lt n$$$), and subtract $$$\\min(a_i,a_{i+1})$$$ from both $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_{i+1}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine if it is possible to make the sequence "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-decreasing"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" by using the operation any number of times."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible to make the sequence "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-decreasing"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on a new line. Otherwise, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on a new line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case. For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will also be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n5\n1 2 3 4 5\n4\n4 3 2 1\n4\n4 5 2 3\n8\n4 5 4 5 4 5 4 5\n9\n9 9 8 2 4 4 3 5 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the array is already sorted."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, we can show that it is impossible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, after performing an operation on $$$i=1$$$, the array becomes $$$[0,1,2,3]$$$, which is now in nondecreasing order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"2060D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2060/problem/D"}